{"w":2400,"h":3396,"lines":[{"x":0.076131685562318835,"y":0.033430232413812155,"t":"Audioscripts","w":0.12139918009440104,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1},{"h":0.013081395583944611,"x":0.080246918237271148,"y":0.077034883594292225,"w":0.69341562906901044,"c":1,"t":"So it looks as if the dodo was better able to survive and defend itself than was originally"},{"c":1,"y":0.092201410199799216,"x":0.080173146769185452,"h":0.016193713400473486,"t":"believed. Yet less than 200 years after Europeans first arrived on the island, they had","w":0.67506627400716146},{"w":0.68130874633789062,"h":0.017807649358562938,"y":0.10710334100769814,"x":0.080140287186376377,"c":1,"t":"become extinct. So what was the reason for this? For a long time, it was believed that"},{"t":"the dodos were hunted to extinction, but scientists now believe the situation was more","w":0.68336232503255212,"x":0.080131724947663421,"h":0.018038746324950283,"y":0.12195757459011414,"c":1},{"t":"complicated than this. Another factor may have been the new species brought to the island","c":1,"x":0.08017308885270448,"y":0.13791291205054201,"w":0.72031880696614581,"h":0.015826777940082914},{"x":0.080166057180807299,"w":0.72649291992187504,"y":0.15360321392070952,"h":0.016080010484890828,"c":1,"t":"by the sailors. These included dogs, which would have been a threat to the dodos, and also"},{"h":0.016345436356794973,"w":0.71829299926757817,"t":"monkeys, which ate the fruit that was the main part of the dodos' diet. These were brought","x":0.080155785314599659,"c":1,"y":0.16862409407252321},{"t":"to the island deliberately, but the ships also brought another type of creature - rats, which","y":0.18359458599020417,"h":0.019105810158665415,"x":0.07806289271446587,"c":1,"w":0.71219904581705729},{"w":0.71810699462890626,"x":0.08024691424657969,"y":0.20053003554006732,"c":1,"h":0.013250883392226132,"t":"came to land from the ships and rapidly overran the island. These upset the ecology of the"},{"t":"island, not just the dodos but other species too. However, they were a particular danger to the","y":0.21512458198028517,"w":0.74705485026041663,"x":0.078131838657929692,"c":1,"h":0.016357615081104226},{"t":"dodos because they consumed their eggs, and since each dodo only laid one at a time, this","y":0.23110465102874733,"h":0.014534883982160851,"x":0.08024690412047733,"w":0.72839508056640623,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.3950617218017578,"y":0.24852767952789634,"h":0.013100227562642619,"t":"probably had a devastating effect on populations.","x":0.080246916779930857},{"c":1,"y":0.26785237501786074,"t":"However, we now think that probably the main cause of the birds' extinction was not the","x":0.082188357610687324,"w":0.69364100138346352,"h":0.017464830400806042},{"x":0.07818930300020184,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"introduction of non-native species, but the introduction of agriculture. This meant that the","y":0.28474676067946858,"w":0.70576131184895829},{"t":"forest that had once covered all the island, and that had provided a perfect home for the","x":0.080246917104718138,"y":0.30087209290034078,"w":0.69958847045898442,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"c":1,"w":0.72858169555664065,"y":0.31536402587033352,"x":0.080162486455111828,"t":"dodo, was cut down so that crops such as sugar could be grown. So although the dodo had","h":0.016745038813219204},{"t":"survived for thousands of years, suddenly it was gone.","x":0.078066011577518857,"w":0.43849578857421873,"h":0.019412832630817944,"c":1,"y":0.33084371685493741},{"t":"Q39","y":0.18313953470076028,"w":0.037037035624186143,"c":1,"x":0.84979423934840082,"h":0.013081395583944611},{"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"Q40","x":0.84979423929272424,"y":0.29941860449513436,"w":0.037037035624186143,"c":1},{"x":0.084362140527292032,"y":0.90552325565792502,"c":1,"w":0.037037035624186199,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"120"},{"x":0.71922402793715989,"w":0.25061218261718743,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","c":1,"y":0.9561987124207002,"h":0.02906125116966074}]}